<Prose title="Terms of Use | All Metal Brake" description="The terms for using All Metal Brake: how you may use our backup power guides, the limits of our advice, prices, affiliate links and third-party sites." h1="Terms of Use" path="/terms/">
  <h2>Using This Site</h2>
  <p>The guides here are free to read. You are welcome to quote a short passage with a link back. Republishing a guide in full, or feeding our content to a scraper, is not permitted.</p>
  <h2>Our Advice Has Limits</h2>
  <p>We research products and report what we find, but we cannot know your specific circuit, fuel supply, climate or local building code. Nothing here is professional advice. Follow the manufacturer's instructions, and where work involves electricity, gas or connecting a generator to your home, use a licensed professional.</p>
  <p>Generators produce carbon monoxide and fuel is flammable. Where we flag a safety point, treat it as the minimum rather than the whole of it.</p>
  <h2>Prices and Availability</h2>
  <p>We do not quote prices. The retailer's listing is always the authority on price, availability and current specification.</p>
  <h2>Affiliate Relationships</h2>
  <p>We earn commission on some outbound links, including as a participant in the Amazon Services LLC Associates Program. Commission does not affect rankings. Details are in our <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.</p>
  <h2>Third-Party Sites</h2>
  <p>We link to retailers and manufacturers. We do not control those sites and are not responsible for their content, prices or privacy practices.</p>
  <h2>Trademarks</h2>
  <p>Product and brand names are the property of their owners. Naming a product in a guide does not imply any endorsement of this site by its manufacturer.</p>
  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about these terms go to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.</p>
</Prose>
